From: Jordan <dev.in@gnu6.live>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:36:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(placement): engine-reported layer placement, explicit
 GPU layer count, native-path sizing test

- DeviceMapSetting::into_mapper reports the placement it built to
  GNOSTRAL_PLACEMENT_OUT (gnostral-trace feature): per-layer devices, the
  non-mapped device and a canonical string such as 0-15:cuda:0,16-47:cpu;nm=cuda:0.
- gnostral_capture --gpu-layers N pins an explicit map; it prints
  GNOSTRAL_PLACEMENT <canonical> and records it in the capture's lane.
- Test that walks the native GGUF path (archive, descriptor, adapter,
  synthesized config, GGUF weight source, pack factor) and checks that the
  device-map sizing drops host-loaded expert stacks; it fails without 0007.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016D4Xz7aLLGu873oZNF6vk4
